    "Micronaut existing image125120183bytes used the current eight-range CDN path: imageDownload7682ms including CDN6558ms; Docker load2894ms; health20875ms, product21632ms, write22556ms. One successful range download, no origin/fallback.",
    "Cached Ktor health7029ms/product7585ms/write8473ms; cached Micronaut health9056ms/product9516ms/write10375ms. SQLite2\u21923\u21924 and18\u219219\u219220 survived reload and full application stop/relaunch.",
    "Existing preparation publishes images to private storage only during a build. README explicitly leaves legacy artifacts on origin until re-preparation. Migrating already-prepared images can enable CDN delivery without recompiling or changing their immutable artifact identity.",
    "Storage setup cannot simply run wholesale before image preparation: persistentVolumes may create migration helper containers from a service image. No speculative startup parallelism was deployed."
